Article 17 An environmental impact report on a construction project shall include the following:
(1) a general description of the construction project;
(2) the current environmental status around the construction project;
(3) analysis, prediction and assessment of the possible environmental impacts of the construction project;
(4) environmental protection measures for the construction project and their technical and economic justification;
(5) an economic cost-benefit analysis of the environmental impact of the construction project;
(6) recommendations for environmental monitoring during the implementation of the construction project; and
(7) conclusions of the environmental impact assessment.
The content and format of the environmental impact statement and the environmental impact registration form shall be prescribed by the competent department of ecology and environment of the State Council.
